 "script": "Guests are coming in an hour. And the furnace just... stopped.\n\nNo problem. One good kick!\n\nOw! My foot! Still nothing.\n\nDing dong! Come in, come in. Keep your coats on.\n\nA gas furnace usually lasts about fifteen to twenty years.\n\nOne. Check the easy stuff: thermostat on heat with fresh batteries, the furnace switch on, and a clean filter.\n\nTwo. Find your home warranty or manufacturer warranty, and read what's covered and the service fee.\n\nThree. Smell gas? Get everyone out and call the gas company. No gas smell? Book a licensed tech, and get the quote in writing.\n\nIf Homie can figure it out, so can you.",
 "audio_note": "Revid voice render was 50.2 s of voice. audio.m4a cuts 'Homie knows the fix.', 'Here's the thing.' and 'So when yours quits on a cold night, do this.' at the quiet gaps between words (30 ms crossfades), trims at 50.9 s and speeds up 1.25x with ffmpeg atempo (pitch kept); caption times shifted and divided by 1.25",
